     2342  [ edit ]
     2343  There are 2,783,247 foreign residents in South Korea as of December 2025, 5.44% of the total population. [ 58 ] Chinese nationals make up approximately one-third of this population (980,670), followed by Vietnamese (337,183), Americans (180,230), Thais (169,848), Uzbeks (102,804), Filipinos (74,125)
     2344  Fair amount of the foreign residents from some countries are Korean descendants. Two thirds of Chinese, half of Russian, one fourth of Uzbeks are repatriated ethnic Koreans (labelled "Overseas Koreans") who may meet criteria for expedited acquisition of South Korean citizenship . They are Korean Chi
     2345  Also, sizeable number of migrants from countries with primarily multicultural immigrant population, such as Australia , New Zealand , Canada , United States , and Japan are also of Korean ethnic descent.
